    "authors": [
      "rules-as-references conformance (esm-spec §9.6.3 constraint 7, §9.6.4 rule 3)"
    ],
    "description": "esm-spec §9.6.3 constraint 7: one rule (`central`) fires at three sites with different operands (`a`, `b`, `2*c`). Each firing writes a reference to the rule bound to what its match captured, so the emitted document holds three references and one materialized body: `central` emitted as a match-less entry in its authored position. Two leaf-bodied rules write their leaf instead of a reference: `dx_const` (body `0.25`) writes the number, `same` (body `u`, a parameter) writes what `u` bound. `expanded.esm` is Expand(load(fixture)), the tree the in-place engine produced.",
    "name": "rule_writes_reference"
  },
